I don't think that we (you, I, and Derek) disagree too much here, it 
seems we're just using different words for the same thing.

However just as you don't think "realism" is the right term, I don't 
think "internal consistency" is either. Firstly, it gives no clues about 
what to do before a ruleset exists: either before the game exists, or 
before a significant new feature is added. Secondly, if all eggs were 
readable but not eatable, that'd be consistent - but it wouldn't be 
intuitive.

